        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2e218d1f-1b3c-55b3-90e8-5a02909c12df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gene Kelly, Rosemary Lane, Liza Minnelli, George Abbott\n- Works: Best Foot Forward, Flora the Red Menace, The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood, Cabaret, Liza with a \"Z\", Lucky Lady, A Matter of Time, New York, New York, The Act, The Rink, Stepping Out, Music from The Life: A New Musical, Sex and the City 2\n- Roles: director, choreographer, performer, recording artist\n\nFacts:\n- Gene Kelly was born on August 23, 1912, and he was an American dancer, actor for film, stage, and television, singer, film director, producer, and choreographer.\n- Best Foot Forward was directed by George Abbott, choreographed by Gene Kelly, and starred Rosemary Lane.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to the original cast recording of Best Foot Forward in 1963.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to original cast recordings or soundtrack albums for Flora the Red Menace and The Dangerous Christmas of Red Riding Hood in 1965.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to soundtrack albums for Cabaret and Liza with a \"Z\" in 1972.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to soundtrack albums for Lucky Lady in 1975, A Matter of Time in 1976, and New York, New York and The Act in 1977.\n- Liza Minnelli contributed to soundtrack albums or cast recordings for The Rink in 1984, Stepping Out in 1991, Music from The Life: A New Musical in 1995, and Sex and the City 2 in 2010.\n- Gene Kelly died on February 2, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
